/**

@page applications_exahype2_shallow_water_tafjord_landslide Landslide on the Tafjord Region of Norway

We also simulate a landslide-generated tsunami in Tafjord using the nonlinear shallow-water
equations within the ExaHyPE 2 framework. This test case represents an idealised model of
a rapid mass movement into a fjord and the resulting long-wave motion.
At \f$ t=0 \f$ the water depth \f$ h \f$ is set equal to the sampled displacement and the bed
elevation \f$ z \f$ is given by the digital elevation model, yielding a data-driven initial condition that
captures the complex geometry of the fjord and the imposed wave or slide footprint.
All other flow variables are initially zero. At the open boundaries the solution is simply
copied from inside to outside, corresponding to non-reflective boundary conditions that allow
waves to leave the computational domain with minimal spurious reflection.

![Tafjord Google Earth Image](Tafjord_GoogleEarth.png)

<p align="center">
  <img src="tafjord-landslide.gif" />
</p>

*/
